# 03 — Findings, Verdict Criteria, Rounds, and Report

> Topic: Unified BLOCKER/MAJOR/MINOR finding table, no-waiver policy, verdict thresholds, 3-round cap, delta re-review, and report format (`R7`–`R8`, `R10`–`R14`)

<!-- GEN: Why: shared severity definitions, strict no-waiver rules, and a fixed report schema prevent endless negotiation and preserve an auditable review trail. Kind: Mandatory. -->

## 1. Unified Finding Severity & Row Format (`R8`, `R12`)

Every finding uses `RV-NN` (kept across rounds) and the unified 3-tier scale (`BLOCKER` / `MAJOR` / `MINOR`):

| ID | Pass | Severity | Confidence | File:line | Problem | Failure scenario / evidence | Fix direction |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `RV-01` | 6 rubric | `BLOCKER` | `CONFIRMED` | `{{example_path}}:42` | `<Rule ID>`: One sentence naming the violation or defect | Command output, validator error, or `given → when → then` scenario | What must change, not the replacement code |

- Put the rule ID first in `Problem` for rubric violations (e.g., `DOM-001: Domain entity imports ORM`), or keep the failure scenario for `2 bug-hunt` rows.
- Pure cleanup or refactoring suggestions without a defect or rule breach are listed below the table as `NOTE: <path:line> — <cleanup>` for `code-simplification` and never block (`R12`).

---

## 2. No Reviewer Waivers & Plan Conflicts (`R7`)

- **No Reviewer Waivers:** The Reviewer cannot excuse an architecture, security, or rubric violation regardless of technical rationale.
- **When a Finding Conflicts with the Plan (`PLAN_CONFLICT`):** If fixing a violation requires changing a locked decision (`D-NN`), API contract, or frozen phase scope, mark the finding `PLAN_CONFLICT` in the report and route it to Planning (`change-control`) rather than instructing the Code Writer to deviate on their own.

---

## 3. Verdict Criteria (`R10`)

| Verdict | Required Conditions |
|---|---|
| `APPROVED` | Every re-run check is `PASS`; every applicable phase AC is traced to implementation and a passing check; `bug-hunt` left no `CONFIRMED` `BLOCKER` or `MAJOR`; zero rubric `BLOCKER` or `MAJOR` findings; required validators clean; visual evidence `PASS` when UI is affected |
| `CHANGES_REQUESTED` | Any `CONFIRMED` `BLOCKER` or `MAJOR` (from `bug-hunt` or rubric passes), any `FAIL` gate, any untraced AC, `TEST-TAMPER-001`, or an open `PLAN_CONFLICT` |
| `BLOCKED` | Missing Gate 1–3 approvals, unresolvable/moving revision, a required check/environment that cannot run, or a `PLAUSIBLE` `BLOCKER` awaiting external evidence |

---

## 4. Rounds, Delta Re-Review & Revision-Bound Report (`R11`, `R13`, `R14`)

- **Delta Re-Review (`R14`):** Each fix creates a new `REVIEW_REVISION`. Inspect `previous_REVIEW_REVISION..new_REVIEW_REVISION`, verify every finding claimed `FIXED` or `DISPUTED` (`review-resolution`), and rerun all affected gates on the new tree.
- **3-Round Cap (`R11`):** Maximum 3 review rounds per phase. If round 3 is still not `APPROVED`, stop and escalate with both positions documented.
- **Report Location (`R13`):** Write the report to `{{report_location}}` (`vN/reviews/review_<phase-id>_<REVIEW_REVISION>.md`), recording:
  1. Revision header (`BASE_REVISION`, `REVIEW_REVISION`, uncommitted scope, Gate 1–3 references, overall verdict & round)
  2. Re-run gate & validator evidence rows (`PASS` / `FAIL`)
  3. Acceptance criteria traceability table
  4. `bug-hunt` pass summary & rows
  5. Five-axis rubric assessment & `RV-NN` findings table
  6. Runtime visual review gate (`PASS` / `FAIL` / `N/A`) and hand-off action

